# Copy to .env, which Git refuses to track:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Read by `uvicorn sinhala_reader.serve:app`. The real environment always wins,
# so a value exported in your shell or set by a deployment overrides this file
# and a stale copy cannot quietly take over a server.
#
# Every setting here is read once at start-up. An unrecognised value stops the
# process rather than quietly serving something else: a typo in a deployment
# variable must not silently change what readers get.
#
# `GET /readiness` reports the mode each of these resolved to, and every way the
# running server is not production. It is the answer to "what is this deployment
# actually doing", not this file.
#
# Never commit .env. scripts/verify-repo-hygiene.sh fails the build if you do.

# ---- Identity -------------------------------------------------------------
# development = trust an X-Reader-User header. Anyone can claim to be anyone;
#               never expose such a server.
# sessions    = real accounts, registration and login.
# Unset means the API refuses to serve at all, which is deliberate.
#
# Note that `sessions` is not yet a finished account system: there is no rate
# limiting, no email verification and no password reset. /readiness says so.
SINHALA_READER_AUTH=development

# Origins a browser may call the API from, comma separated. Unset means none.
SINHALA_READER_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000

# ---- Voice ----------------------------------------------------------------
# development = a labelled placeholder tone. xtts = the real checkpoint.
# An unrecognised value stops the process rather than quietly serving tones.
SINHALA_READER_TTS=development
# cpu or cuda. Unset lets the adapter choose.
# SINHALA_READER_TTS_DEVICE=cpu
# Where the model bundle is. Never inside this repository.
# SINHALA_TTS_MODEL_DIR=/path/to/xtts_si_female

# ---- Storage and queue ----------------------------------------------------
# Unset means in memory: everything is lost when the process stops.
# SINHALA_READER_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://reader:dev@127.0.0.1:55432/reader
# Unset means a thread per job: work in flight is lost if the process stops.
# SINHALA_READER_QUEUE=celery
# SINHALA_READER_REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:56379/0

# ---- Document structure ---------------------------------------------------
# A model may infer structure over text already extracted - block roles,
# reading order, boundaries - and may never supply the words themselves. Its
# output is reassembled and compared character for character against the
# extraction it was given; one altered character rejects the page. See the
# "Structure may be inferred by a model; words may not" section of CLAUDE.md.
#
# Sending a reader's document to an external provider is external processing.
# Unset means the deterministic path, which must stay shippable on its own.
# SINHALA_READER_STRUCTURE=gemini
# SINHALA_READER_STRUCTURE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ---- Reading a page from its image ----------------------------------------
# off    = never. A page whose embedded text cannot be decoded stays unread.
# broken = only pages whose text layer failed. Every other page keeps its exact
#          embedded text, which recognition could only make worse.
# all    = every page. Consistent, slower, and adds recognition errors to pages
#          that did not need them.
#
# Tesseract runs on this server, so unlike structure and answers nothing leaves
# the machine. It must be installed with its Sinhala data (`sin`); the container
# images install it, and compose sets `broken`. Unset means off, because a
# contributor's machine usually has no Tesseract and recognition adds seconds
# per page.
#
# Recognised text can misread letters, and those pages are marked as not
# checked. There is no review or correction workflow yet.
# SINHALA_READER_OCR=broken
# The executable, if it is not on PATH as `tesseract`.
# SINHALA_READER_TESSERACT=/usr/bin/tesseract

# ---- Study answers --------------------------------------------------------
# extractive = passages from the book, in the book's own words. Needs no
#              provider, no key and no network, and abstains whenever the
#              question's wording does not match the text - which is often.
#              This is what makes study mode shippable without a contract.
# gemini     = answers written in Sinhala by an external model, which means the
#              passages retrieved for each question are sent to Google. Cited
#              passages are checked to be ones actually retrieved, so a citation
#              cannot be invented; the prose itself is not verified.
#
# Needs GEMINI_API_KEY above.
# SINHALA_READER_ANSWERS=gemini
# The model that writes the answer. Pinned, not a `-latest` alias, because the
# version string reaches provenance. Not selected by evaluation - CLAUDE.md
# asks for that and it has not been done.
# SINHALA_READER_ANSWER_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash
# The model that turns a question into search terms, and the answer model's
# stand-in when it is rate-limited.
# SINHALA_READER_PLAN_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# ---- Vendored data --------------------------------------------------------
# Where the FM-Abhaya legacy-font tables are. Found relative to the package by
# default; set this only when the data is mounted elsewhere, as it is in a
# worker container that does not have the repository laid out around it.
# SINHALA_LEGACY_FONT_DIR=/app/data/legacy_fonts
